Third-party and vendored material
----------------------------------

HAL's KONO memory substrate (lib/hal/kono/) is a vendored, standalone
simplification of the equivalent module in CodeTonight's own GRIP project
(https://github.com/grip-platform/GRIP), under the same copyright holder
and the same licence (AGPL-3.0-only). This is not third-party code; it is
noted here for provenance only.

A small number of files (lib/hal/tool_dispatch.py, parts of
lib/hal/cost_tracker.py, and parts of lib/hal/memory_engine.py) carry
in-code comments attributing design or data to a project referred to in
those comments as "TF++". That material is credited to Thomas Frumkin.
CodeTonight's operator confirmed on 2026-11-22 that it may ship as part
of this open-source release with that credit. No other licence terms for
this material are stated or implied beyond that confirmation. Questions
about this attribution can be sent to licensing@codetonight.co.za.

No other third-party source code is vendored into this repository as of
the date of this release candidate. Third-party LLM provider APIs, models
and services that HAL connects to at runtime (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google,
Groq, xAI, DeepSeek, Alibaba/DashScope, Mistral, and others) are accessed
over their own published interfaces under their own terms, are not
distributed with this software, and are not covered by this NOTICE.
